  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Friday)\nIssued at 901 PM CST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nHigh pressure will build into the Tennessee Valley next week,\npromoting tranquil weather and a gradual warming trend, along with\ndry conditions. This will result in mostly sunny conditions each \nday, resulting beautiful autumn weather for early November. Highs\nin the upper 60s to perhaps lower 70s will be common by Tuesday \nand Wednesday. Later in the week, a broad upper low over the Great\nLakes will send a couple of shortwave troughs and their associated\ndry fronts into the area. These features will bring reinforcing\nshots of cooler, drier air into the area, knocking highs back into\nthe upper 50s to lower 60s and lows into the low to mid 30s.\nHowever, no precipitation is forecast to accompany these \nfeatures, with some added cloud cover the only noticeable change \nto the weather.",
